	(paper "A4")
	(title_block
		(title "MV Telescope electrical: sheet map")
		(date "2026-11-06")
		(rev "v2")
		(company "MV Astronomy")
		(comment 1 "Each block is one owner's sheet file. Double-click a block to open it.")
		(comment 2 "The wires on this page are the agreed connections between sheets.")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "Pi → HAT: the 17 Pi signals from the pin map.     HAT → power: the 6 buffered lines that run by cable to the two DM542T drivers.\n+5V, +3V3 and GND are power symbols: they join across every sheet on their own, so they need no wire here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1974ace9-3f9a-5b59-a3ff-b85cb3d5ea9e")
	)
	(text "WHO OWNS WHAT (one file each, so nobody edits the same file)\n  •  Pi header  ·  pi_header.kicad_sch  ·  Eeshan  ·  done: J1 + the pin map\n  •  HAT signals  ·  hat_signals.kicad_sch  ·  Ibrahim  ·  74ACT244 buffer, driver / limit / encoder connectors, pull-ups, caps\n  •  Power and drivers  ·  power.kicad_sch  ·  Eeshan for now, open to a new member  ·  battery to DM542Ts (off the PCB)\n  •  This page and the project files (.kicad_pro, .kicad_pcb)  ·  Eeshan\n\nRULES\n  1. Only edit your own sheet file. Open the project, then double-click your block on this page.\n  2. The pins and wires on this page are the contract. Need a new signal between sheets? Ask Eeshan: he adds it here and in both sheets.\n  3. Annotate only your sheet: Tools > Annotate Schematic, scope 'Current sheet only', numbering 'First free after sheet number × 100'.\n      So HAT signals parts become U301, R301, J301...  and power parts F401, SW401...  No two sheets can pick the same reference.\n  4. Power and drivers is set to 'Exclude from board': nothing on it goes on the HAT PCB.\n  5. Every change goes through a GitHub pull request. The ERC check runs on its own and must pass before it merges."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 112 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "57f34cfe-b92c-5ea9-9866-85eca1d8bcd4")
	)
